From 015f6958f482fb7cc01c0d18b6a4423d5ed4350f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:53:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] notices: pollers of one replica snapshot share a
 single _persist pass

observe() publishes its memo only after _persist commits, outside the replica
lane and the publication lock. Every notice poller that arrived meanwhile found
no memo for the new signature and re-ran the whole pass over every terminal
card, queueing on the ledger's BEGIN IMMEDIATE. On hermes-hub (11-13, 5-7
pollers per backend, 9318 remote task rows, 6286 terminal) remote notice
collection was 25% of the gateway's and 34% of the Desktop backend's CPU; a
harness with 7 pollers and a 0.6 s pass ran _persist 79 times for 21 replica
changes.

A caller whose snapshot has the same signature, replica file and ledger file
as a pass in flight now waits for that pass and returns its answer, the one a
memo hit would return. The memo is re-read in the second lock block so a
caller that missed it in the first look does not re-persist. A leader always
sets its event in finally; if it failed, each waiter persists once itself
(no follow on retry). Snapshots without a signature or file identity never
share. Generation ordering and the out-of-lock ledger write are unchanged.

Tests: one pass for 7 concurrent polls; leader failure with 1 and 3 waiters
terminates and answers each; a newer snapshot does not wait for an older one;
_reset_for_tests never strands a waiter; the 12-caller single-flight test now
also pins one ledger pass.

